.","The hypothetical if-clause uses past-form **measured** to mark distance from reality.","Choose **measured**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"An -ing form alone is not a finite clause verb.","B":"The hypothetical if-clause uses past-form **measured** to mark distance from reality.","C":"The requested second-conditional if-clause uses a past form, not present -s.","D":"Would belongs in the result clause in this standard pattern."}}},{"id":"ba0f0dc8-d359-5c27-a8f2-7f2790b14247","topicSlug":"conditionals","level":"B1","prompt":"Complete the second-conditional result: “If I had more time now, I ____ the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"would measuring"},{"id":"B","text":"would measure"},{"id":"C","text":"would to measure"},{"id":"D","text":"would measured"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Match **if + past** with **would + base verb** in this standard hypothetical pattern.","explanation":"An imagined present result takes **would + measure**.","keywords":["second-result"],"skill":"second-result","contextKey":"conditionals-3","fingerprint":"e0e2834c18e83a998280570f5c075cbdcc261c57359d1ab939c1abe34c30ee9d","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-conditionals"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Match **if + past** with **would + base verb** in this standard hypothetical pattern.","An imagined present result takes **would + measure**.","Choose **would measure**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Would needs be before -ing; this task asks for the simple result pattern.","B":"An imagined present result takes **would + measure**.","C":"Would takes a bare infinitive without to.","D":"A past form cannot directly follow would."}}},{"id":"794544ad-d5d5-5431-abd4-70e2b446b5e2","topicSlug":"conditionals","level":"B1","prompt":"State a regular procedure in the zero conditional: “Whenever an order arrives, she ____ the travel leaflet.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"translate"},{"id":"B","text":"will to translate"},{"id":"C","text":"translating"},{"id":"D","text":"translates"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"A **regular procedure** uses present simple in both clauses; then check subject–verb agreement.","explanation":"This describes a repeated procedure, so the zero-conditional result uses present simple **translates**, agreeing with she.","keywords":["zero-result"],"skill":"zero-result","contextKey":"conditionals-4","fingerprint":"fbed61bb93386433f510811efb04955e1d03986c94d856c7f691a69c7e61532b","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-conditionals"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["A **regular procedure** uses present simple in both clauses; then check subject–verb agreement.","This describes a repeated procedure, so the zero-conditional result uses present simple **translates**, agreeing with she.","Choose **translates**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The present-simple verb needs third-person -s with she.","B":"Will cannot be followed by to; the task also asks for a regular present procedure.","C":"An -ing form alone is not a finite verb for this result.","D":"This describes a repeated procedure, so the zero-conditional result uses present simple **translates**, agreeing with she."}}},{"id":"840cd099-9182-5441-aa30-b7a3d26669f2","topicSlug":"conditionals","level":"B1","prompt":"Use the standard first conditional: “If she ____ the travel leaflet tomorrow, we will be ready.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"translates"},{"id":"B","text":"will translate"},{"id":"C","text":"would translate"},{"id":"D","text":"translating"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"This is a **real future possibility**; use pr